{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And all the congregation of the children of Israel complained.</b> After two punishments had been done among them — swallowing and burning — what was left for them to complain about, that they would not believe with complete faith?" "<b>But</b> the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: the correct interpretation is that after the burning they did believe in the priesthood of Aharon, for fire had already gone out from before HaShem and consumed his offerings; but Israel desired that the firstborn serve the Tabernacle in place of the Levites, and they were unwilling to accept the exchange that was made concerning them, for they wanted all the tribes to have a share in the service of the House of HaShem. And now they complain: <b>You have killed the people of HaShem</b> — for you gave this counsel that they bring incense like priests, when they were fit for the service of the Levites, not to be like priests offering incense. And this is the reason the staff of Ahaver bloomed for the house of Levi. Thus far."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:28.062366789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}